1984
01:46:03,880 --> 01:46:04,660
Hot soup!

1985
01:46:05,000 --> 01:46:05,500
Excuse me!

1986
01:46:05,780 --> 01:46:06,320
Sorry!

1987
01:46:07,140 --> 01:46:08,120
By the way...

1988
01:46:09,860 --> 01:46:11,120
I'm not a villager!

1989
01:46:11,860 --> 01:46:12,400
Ha ha ha!

1990
01:46:12,840 --> 01:46:13,380
Got him!

1991
01:46:14,480 --> 01:46:15,240
No- Oh shit!

1992
01:46:16,740 --> 01:46:20,820
Wait, where's the- Hold on guys, I'll be out of your face.

1993
01:46:22,640 --> 01:46:23,400
Here we go!

1994
01:46:24,000 --> 01:46:25,740
Yep, I'll see you later.

1995
01:46:27,660 --> 01:46:28,380
Okay.

1996
01:46:28,800 --> 01:46:29,900
That was awesome!

1997
01:46:30,280 --> 01:46:31,760
What the heck, man?

1998
01:46:32,580 --> 01:46:34,560
I can't believe all that stuff is possible!

1999
01:46:34,940 --> 01:46:37,700
When you make a freaking Minecraft map!

2000
01:46:38,060 --> 01:46:38,780
What?!

2001
01:46:38,780 --> 01:46:40,840
How is that possible?

2002
01:46:41,620 --> 01:46:41,940
Jeff.

2003
01:46:44,400 --> 01:46:44,900
How's it going?

2004
01:46:46,560 --> 01:46:47,220
Don't mind me.

2005
01:46:48,020 --> 01:46:48,940
I have a date.

2006
01:46:49,240 --> 01:46:49,980
With a llama.

2007
01:46:51,040 --> 01:46:51,880
Actually, four of them.

2008
01:46:54,020 --> 01:46:54,740
Let's go over there.

2009
01:46:55,280 --> 01:46:56,240
Let me turn this down a bit again.

2010
01:46:59,600 --> 01:47:00,000
Okay.

2011
01:47:00,300 --> 01:47:01,140
Back to the mine!

2012
01:47:03,120 --> 01:47:04,820
Let me see the achievements here.

2013
01:47:06,220 --> 01:47:06,820
Yeah!

2014
01:47:07,400 --> 01:47:09,300
We found four llamas!

2015
01:47:10,740 --> 01:47:11,760
There they are!

2016
01:47:11,900 --> 01:47:12,440
Look at that!

2017
01:47:13,620 --> 01:47:14,600
It's beautiful!

2018
01:47:18,520 --> 01:47:19,120
Great!

2019
01:47:19,400 --> 01:47:19,980
They're all here!

2020
01:47:21,020 --> 01:47:21,260
Yeah!

2021
01:47:22,500 --> 01:47:24,240
Time to put these llamas to work!

2022
01:47:24,520 --> 01:47:24,880
That's right!

2023
01:47:25,200 --> 01:47:25,680
Also-

2024
01:47:29,500 --> 01:47:30,320
What happened?

2025
01:47:33,340 --> 01:47:33,940
Oh!

2026
01:47:35,320 --> 01:47:36,340
Thanks for the help.

2027
01:47:37,840 --> 01:47:38,880
No, no worries.

2028
01:47:39,100 --> 01:47:41,560
I almost got my head, uh, slapped by a big rock.

2029
01:47:42,920 --> 01:47:43,400
Okay.

2030
01:47:43,640 --> 01:47:44,680
Um, now...

2031
01:47:44,680 --> 01:47:45,060
What is this?

2032
01:47:46,180 --> 01:47:46,660
Wait!

2033
01:47:46,760 --> 01:47:47,540
New recipes unlocked!

2034
01:47:49,460 --> 01:47:49,940
Oh!

2035
01:47:50,100 --> 01:47:50,940
Check recipe book!

2036
01:47:52,100 --> 01:47:52,580
Oh!

2037
01:47:53,220 --> 01:47:53,460
A...

2038
01:47:56,140 --> 01:47:58,260
Now with 30% more sea pickles?

2039
01:48:00,540 --> 01:48:01,520
That's not a thing.

2040
01:48:02,940 --> 01:48:03,980
I will make one.

2041
01:48:07,330 --> 01:48:08,190
That's amazing.

2042
01:48:11,450 --> 01:48:11,950
Ew!

2043
01:48:12,110 --> 01:48:12,570
It's wet!

2044
01:48:13,430 --> 01:48:13,930
Strength.

2045
01:48:15,310 --> 01:48:16,310
Oh, shit.

2046
01:48:16,470 --> 01:48:16,610
Okay.

2047
01:48:17,610 --> 01:48:18,650
Let's keep that in mind.

2048
01:48:19,010 --> 01:48:20,070
Maybe we need to make another one.

2049
01:48:21,210 --> 01:48:22,730
So what's down here in the mines?

2050
01:48:27,000 --> 01:48:27,900
Let me see here.

2051
01:48:30,160 --> 01:48:30,660
Oh!

2052
01:48:42,690 --> 01:48:43,530
What's this?

2053
01:48:47,010 --> 01:48:49,590
This extraction station was built many years ago.

2054
01:48:50,030 --> 01:48:52,250
I remember when we first found this area.

2055
01:48:52,490 --> 01:48:55,170
More iron than any of us had seen in our lifetimes.

2056
01:48:55,330 --> 01:48:56,130
Oh, yeah!

2057
01:48:57,190 --> 01:48:58,590
Nowadays, it's more of a hut.

2058
01:48:59,430 --> 01:49:00,930
Rarely anyone comes by here anymore.

2059
01:49:01,930 --> 01:49:03,430
I used to be beautiful here.

2060
01:49:04,270 --> 01:49:06,630
Lush caves, mineral glistening at every corner.

2061
01:49:07,870 --> 01:49:08,310
It.

2062
01:49:08,530 --> 01:49:09,290
Not I.

2063
01:49:09,610 --> 01:49:10,810
Me, Henry and Gary.

2064
01:49:11,090 --> 01:49:12,930
My co-workers and best friends I've ever had.

2065
01:49:13,170 --> 01:49:14,690
We had such great fun in here.

2066
01:49:14,890 --> 01:49:17,450
Away from all our responsibilities back on the surface.

2067
01:49:18,950 --> 01:49:23,030
Once we delved all the minerals here, they moved on to newer, deeper areas.

2068
01:49:23,630 --> 01:49:25,790
I just couldn't bring myself to continue with them.

2069
01:49:26,250 --> 01:49:27,690
It was too beautiful here.

2070
01:49:28,290 --> 01:49:29,870
I've been keeping the place clean.

2071
01:49:30,190 --> 01:49:31,950
Keeping the zombies away most days.

2072
01:49:32,770 --> 01:49:34,470
Other days, I lock myself.

2073
01:49:35,370 --> 01:49:38,250
In, hoping they won't find their way through the copper grate.

2074
01:49:38,510 --> 01:49:40,790
My only access to fresh oxygen in here.

2075
01:49:41,370 --> 01:49:45,970
If you read this, and I'm still alive, you can probably find me chilling on my porch.

2076
01:49:46,530 --> 01:49:47,130
Oh, yeah?

2077
01:49:47,490 --> 01:49:49,070
If not, well...

2078
01:49:49,070 --> 01:49:52,450
There should be more iron down the tunnels, near the deeper stations.

2079
01:49:53,030 --> 01:49:55,310
I haven't heard from anyone down there in months, though.

2080
01:49:55,690 --> 01:49:57,550
So I hope you're not prepared for the worst.

2081
01:49:58,770 --> 01:49:59,490
Poop Man.

2082
01:50:01,650 --> 01:50:03,170
That's his name, Poop Man?!

2083
01:50:03,890 --> 01:50:06,610
After all that serious talk, and then... Poop Man.

2084
01:50:07,530 --> 01:50:08,950
Oh, oh, you're right here.

2085
01:50:10,350 --> 01:50:11,450
I thought I was...

2086
01:50:11,450 --> 01:50:12,310
Hello, Poop Man.

2087
01:50:13,670 --> 01:50:14,150
Oh!

2088
01:50:15,030 --> 01:50:15,370
Whoa!

2089
01:50:15,950 --> 01:50:17,510
You scared the shit out of me!

2090
01:50:19,370 --> 01:50:20,310
That's what I do.

2091
01:50:20,770 --> 01:50:21,730
Well, um...

2092
01:50:21,730 --> 01:50:22,410
Hello there!

2093
01:50:23,030 --> 01:50:27,290
I don't see many visitors, and most that I do see aren't quite alive, so...

2094
01:50:27,730 --> 01:50:28,110
Welcome!

2095
01:50:28,870 --> 01:50:32,730
If you happen to be looking for iron, continue on down the abyss.

2096
01:50:33,870 --> 01:50:35,830
Otherwise, feel free to stay here.

2097
01:50:37,170 --> 01:50:40,190
Please don't read my diary- I mean diary, though.

2098
01:50:41,190 --> 01:50:42,310
I will...

2099
01:50:42,310 --> 01:50:43,810
I will read your diarrhea.

2100
01:50:43,810 --> 01:50:45,030
I will get in there.

2101
01:50:45,450 --> 01:50:45,890
I will get in there.

2102
01:50:45,890 --> 01:50:46,710
And I will see it all.

2103
01:50:48,370 --> 01:50:49,430
I brought my scope.

2104
01:50:50,170 --> 01:50:50,610
Bend over.

2105
01:50:51,530 --> 01:50:52,330
Let me have a look.

2106
01:50:53,910 --> 01:50:54,670
Be aware!

2107
01:50:55,030 --> 01:50:56,390
Gravity is strong in these mines.

2108
01:50:57,050 --> 01:50:57,490
What?!

2109
01:50:59,450 --> 01:51:00,550
The Dark Descent.

2110
01:51:01,610 --> 01:51:02,210
Oh no.

2111
01:51:04,630 --> 01:51:06,150
Obtain iron from the mine.

2112
01:51:07,390 --> 01:51:07,650
Obtain iron from the mine.

2113
01:51:08,310 --> 01:51:08,890
Hmm...

2114
01:51:08,890 --> 01:51:10,330
Abyssal Descent to the left.

2115
01:51:10,550 --> 01:51:11,970
Amethyst Core to the right.

2116
01:51:14,290 --> 01:51:15,410
Amethyst Cove.

2117
01:51:15,510 --> 01:51:15,710
Okay.

2118
01:51:16,510 --> 01:51:17,710
There's a compass here.

2119
01:51:18,370 --> 01:51:18,950
Oh!

2120
01:51:20,170 --> 01:51:21,430
Oh, okay, I see.

2121
01:51:23,030 --> 01:51:24,010
It's very strong.

2122
01:51:24,970 --> 01:51:25,910
Oh, okay.

2123
01:51:27,250 --> 01:51:30,570
It's way stronger than I initially thought, even after I thought it was strong.

2124
01:51:34,550 --> 01:51:35,030
Hmm...

2125
01:51:35,030 --> 01:51:35,950
Uh...

2126
01:51:36,550 --> 01:51:38,070
Maybe I can go here first.

2127
01:51:39,250 --> 01:51:40,130
No, I can't.

2128
01:51:40,250 --> 01:51:42,030
Oh man, I die a lot here.

2129
01:51:42,530 --> 01:51:43,090
Water, water!

2130
01:51:43,850 --> 01:51:45,090
Ah, okay, good, good.

2131
01:51:45,570 --> 01:51:46,250
Of course.

2132
01:51:52,110 --> 01:51:52,590
Okay.

2133
01:51:54,030 --> 01:51:56,030
Let's head to Amethyst Cove.

2134
01:51:56,030 --> 01:51:57,550
Wait, what's down here?

2135
01:51:59,150 --> 01:52:00,470
Old iron mines.

2136
01:52:01,950 --> 01:52:02,270
Oh...

2137
01:52:05,940 --> 01:52:07,720
Let's go to Amethyst Cove first.

2138
01:52:08,320 --> 01:52:09,840
No, we want iron, right?

2139
01:52:10,720 --> 01:52:11,840
Let's head down here.

2140
01:52:11,940 --> 01:52:12,980
No, no, let's go here first.

2141
01:52:13,760 --> 01:52:14,700
Amethyst Cove.

2142
01:52:20,390 --> 01:52:21,030
Note.

2143
01:52:21,510 --> 01:52:23,810
All flowers in storage have been used.

2144
01:52:24,290 --> 01:52:25,990
New extraction necessary.

2145
01:52:26,790 --> 01:52:30,630
For more, try the short-term storage in the geode itself.

2146
01:52:30,630 --> 01:52:32,730
Henry usually leaves some there.

2147
01:52:34,030 --> 01:52:37,570
We really ought to tell that lazy bastard to restock the storage more frequently.

2148
01:52:38,170 --> 01:52:40,110
He always says he will, but never does.

2149
01:52:40,690 --> 01:52:43,150
I reckon he's just scared of going down the cave there.

2150
01:52:43,530 --> 01:52:44,830
But he'd never admit that.

2151
01:52:45,270 --> 01:52:47,730
Always acting like he's the toughest guy of us all.

2152
01:52:49,030 --> 01:52:49,430
Gary.

2153
01:52:50,950 --> 01:52:52,150
I will go down there.

2154
01:52:52,790 --> 01:52:53,590
What is that?

2155
01:52:55,030 --> 01:52:56,030
Oh, it's a bat!

2156
01:52:56,670 --> 01:52:57,770
Couldn't tell what that was.

2157
01:52:58,510 --> 01:52:58,710
Oh!

2158
01:53:05,670 --> 01:53:06,310
Oh no.

2159
01:53:07,610 --> 01:53:08,610
Please don't be scary.

2160
01:53:14,990 --> 01:53:16,690
Oh no, there's gonna be a jump scare.

2161
01:53:20,850 --> 01:53:21,950
Oh, I hate this.

2162
01:53:22,030 --> 01:53:22,590
This is not good.

2163
01:53:27,430 --> 01:53:28,310
Amethyst Cove.

2164
01:53:42,270 --> 01:53:42,670
Oh!

2165
01:53:42,970 --> 01:53:43,330
Henry!

2166
01:53:45,070 --> 01:53:45,470
Wow!

2167
01:53:45,670 --> 01:53:46,190
What's up, man?

2168
01:53:47,610 --> 01:53:48,010
Ah!

2169
01:53:48,210 --> 01:53:48,890
A visitor!

2170
01:53:49,750 --> 01:53:50,530
Yeah, that's right.

2171
01:53:50,930 --> 01:53:54,350
Didn't think anyone else would ever be brave enough to venture through that dark cave.

2172
01:53:55,170 --> 01:53:56,070
Well, here I am.

2173
01:53:56,630 --> 01:53:57,570
Make yourself at home.

2174
01:53:57,830 --> 01:53:58,530
It's nice here.

2175
01:54:00,750 --> 01:54:03,430
And oh yeah, when you go back, take some flowers with you.

2176
01:54:03,830 --> 01:54:04,570
Saves me the hassle.

2177
01:54:05,490 --> 01:54:06,850
Um, okay, hold on.

2178
01:54:06,890 --> 01:54:07,810
Let me turn this down just a bit.

2179
01:54:10,870 --> 01:54:12,230
Uh, do you mind if I read this?

2180
01:54:13,090 --> 01:54:14,130
Henry's Log 4.

2181
01:54:15,250 --> 01:54:16,130
Day 411.

2182
01:54:16,850 --> 01:54:21,650
Today we, uh, stuck some TNT in the small crack in the andeside wall of our storage.

2183
01:54:22,210 --> 01:54:24,070
Turns out there's a whole cave down there.

2184
01:54:24,630 --> 01:54:27,010
It gets pretty dark in there, though, for some reason.

2185
01:54:27,290 --> 01:54:29,490
None of our lamps seem to be able to fully light it up.

2186
01:54:30,710 --> 01:54:32,650
I was the first to dare venture through it.

2187
01:54:32,990 --> 01:54:34,490
Turns out it leads to a dead end.

2188
01:54:34,770 --> 01:54:36,810
A big flat wall of smooth basalt.

2189
01:54:36,810 --> 01:54:39,290
I doubt there's anything of value behind there.

2190
01:54:39,450 --> 01:54:41,430
But we'll tunnel through tomorrow anyways.

2191
01:54:42,310 --> 01:54:42,950
Hold on.

2192
01:54:43,490 --> 01:54:45,330
Make it a little bit quieter still.

2193
01:54:47,110 --> 01:54:47,930
Uh, okay.

2194
01:54:48,690 --> 01:54:49,630
Day 412.

2195
01:54:50,130 --> 01:54:51,290
Well, I was wrong.

2196
01:54:51,470 --> 01:54:52,430
It's beautiful here.

2197
01:54:52,670 --> 01:54:55,030
And these flowers, there's something about them.

2198
01:54:55,330 --> 01:54:57,610
They seem to grow only inside this geode.

2199
01:54:57,790 --> 01:54:58,210
How odd.

2200
01:54:58,770 --> 01:55:00,010
I'll have to show the others.

2201
01:55:01,390 --> 01:55:02,470
Day 413.

2202
01:55:03,250 --> 01:55:05,230
Had some of the boys look at the flowers today.

2203
01:55:05,890 --> 01:55:09,210
Jarek said they remind him of the fireworks they used to light back in his hometown.

2204
01:55:09,490 --> 01:55:10,270
Off the island.

2205
01:55:10,610 --> 01:55:11,730
Seems like a good place.

2206
01:55:12,970 --> 01:55:15,210
Steve and Gary didn't seem to care too much about it.

2207
01:55:15,470 --> 01:55:19,230
Those guys are only here for the minerals and ultimately for the money and it shows.

2208
01:55:19,950 --> 01:55:21,950
I asked Poop Man what he thought of it.

2209
01:55:22,150 --> 01:55:24,550
And he mentioned we could try them as a fuel source.

2210
01:55:25,330 --> 01:55:25,650
Okay.

2211
01:55:26,610 --> 01:55:29,710
Our generators have been running dry lately so we could give it a shot.

2212
01:55:31,470 --> 01:55:32,470
Day 414.

2213
01:55:32,950 --> 01:55:33,910
It's amazing!

2214
01:55:34,190 --> 01:55:34,930
The flowers!

2215
01:55:35,050 --> 01:55:36,910
They're the best fuel source we've ever had!

2216
01:55:37,390 --> 01:55:39,790
It must have something to do with them growing in the geode.

2217
01:55:40,170 --> 01:55:41,610
Absorbing its minerals somehow.

2218
01:55:41,950 --> 01:55:43,370
They burn fantastically.

2219
01:55:44,510 --> 01:55:47,450
From now on these flowers shall be used to power our generators.

2220
01:55:47,910 --> 01:55:52,710
I will schedule periodical extractions and make sure there is always a supply of them in the main storage.

2221
01:55:54,110 --> 01:55:54,930
You do that!

2222
01:55:57,920 --> 01:55:58,780
You do that.

2223
01:56:03,080 --> 01:56:03,440
Henry?

2224
01:56:04,220 --> 01:56:05,800
It's been a while since I saw my friends.

2225
01:56:05,960 --> 01:56:06,880
I wonder what they're up to.

2226
01:56:10,290 --> 01:56:12,890
Didn't you say you needed me to bring back some flowers?

2227
01:56:14,830 --> 01:56:15,650
How do I do that?

2228
01:56:22,820 --> 01:56:24,040
I'm scared of jumping down.

2229
01:56:24,260 --> 01:56:25,200
I think that would be a mistake.

2230
01:56:34,090 --> 01:56:34,450
Oh!

2231
01:56:35,150 --> 01:56:35,730
There we go.

2232
01:56:37,130 --> 01:56:38,090
I'm taking all of them.

2233
01:56:39,750 --> 01:56:40,310
Any more?

2234
01:56:43,480 --> 01:56:44,600
Ah, there we go.

2235
01:56:44,740 --> 01:56:45,060
Even more.

2236
01:56:46,460 --> 01:56:47,980
I think we got...

2237
01:56:47,980 --> 01:56:49,160
All of them.

2238
01:56:49,860 --> 01:56:50,380
Allium.

2239
01:56:51,860 --> 01:56:52,840
That was horrible.

2240
01:56:53,240 --> 01:56:53,400
Hoi!

2241
01:56:54,480 --> 01:56:55,120
Oh no!

2242
01:56:57,230 --> 01:56:59,010
Oh, another death!

2243
01:57:01,870 --> 01:57:03,510
I still have the flowers though.

2244
01:57:04,130 --> 01:57:04,470
Whoops.

2245
01:57:05,290 --> 01:57:06,490
Whoops, whoops, whoops.

2246
01:57:08,270 --> 01:57:09,450
Oh no, not again.

2247
01:57:12,270 --> 01:57:13,630
There's gonna be a jumpscare on the way back.

2248
01:57:19,120 --> 01:57:19,600
I'm ready.

2249
01:57:20,460 --> 01:57:21,540
I'm ready, I'm ready, I'm ready.

2250
01:57:22,400 --> 01:57:22,960
Give it to me.

2251
01:57:25,220 --> 01:57:26,220
Okay, oh nice.

2252
01:57:27,080 --> 01:57:28,060
Yes, good stuff.

2253
01:57:29,000 --> 01:57:30,500
Okay, so we have fuel source now.

2254
01:57:31,880 --> 01:57:32,900
So, uh, Poop Man.

2255
01:57:34,160 --> 01:57:35,000
Did you want this?

2256
01:57:35,280 --> 01:57:36,440
How do I even get up there again?

2257
01:57:38,060 --> 01:57:39,160
Ah, I think I see how.

2258
01:57:42,220 --> 01:57:43,280
Oh no, I can't.

2259
01:57:43,840 --> 01:57:45,560
